WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.840
Hannah: Keep a control group with current settings. Change pooling in the treatment group only.

2
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:13.632
Anika: Okay, same version and sandbox request mix. We can compare like for like.

3
00:00:13.632 --> 00:00:19.703
Lukas: Where does the path MTU test fit? Don't change both variables in one run.

4
00:00:19.703 --> 00:00:27.623
Raj: Separate isolated runs, with saved network settings. We'll dry-run it first without shared traffic.

5
00:00:27.623 --> 00:00:35.663
Priya: Just to confirm, production stays unchanged, right? Both trials start in approved test environments.

6
00:00:35.663 --> 00:00:45.263
Hannah: Yes, report errors and latency together. Include cold starts, idle expiry, and reconnect bursts.

7
00:00:45.263 --> 00:00:52.439
Anika: The rollback trigger is any correctness failure. Resource pressure also stops the pooling trial.

8
00:00:52.439 --> 00:00:59.662
Lukas: Restore the baseline configuration after each run. That keeps the next comparison independent.

9
00:00:59.662 --> 00:01:07.198
Raj: We'll collect roughly an hour per condition. Low sample counts mean extend, not declare success.

10
00:01:07.198 --> 00:01:14.350
Priya: So, document those limits before execution. That makes the proposal ready for ownership.

